Chief Financial Officer (CFO)

Group:
Finance and Strategy
Reports to
: Director General (DG)
Location:
WADA Headquarters, Montreal, Canada

Posting deadline: 11 January 2027

WHO WE ARE

The World Anti-Doping Agency (WADA) was established in 1999 as an international independent agency to lead a collaborative worldwide movement for doping-free sport. As the global regulatory body, WADA’s primary role is to develop, harmonize and coordinate anti-doping rules and policies across all sports and countries. Our key activities include: scientific and social science research; education; intelligence & investigations; development of anti-doping capacity; and, monitoring of compliance with the World Anti-Doping Program.

ABOUT THE ROLE

The Chief Financial Officer (CFO) is a member of WADA’s executive leadership team and is responsible for providing oversight of WADA’s financial management and investment. The CFO safeguards WADA’s long-term financial sustainability and ensures that financial resources are aligned with the Agency’s strategic priorities, mission, and objectives. The role oversees financial planning and analysis, budgeting and forecasting, accounting and reporting, investment and reserves, financial risk management, internal controls, contribution management, and financial compliance.

Working closely with the Director General, Finance and Administration Committee, Risk and Audit Committee and presenting regularly to WADA’s highest governing bodies, the CFO translates WADA’s strategic priorities into sustainable financial and organizational plans and provides insight and analysis to support informed decision-making.
.
WHAT YOU'LL DO

Executive Financial Leadership & Financial Strategy

Develop and lead WADA’s financial strategy in support of its mission, strategic plan, and long-term organizational objectives;
Serve as the principal financial advisor to the Director General, Executive Committee, Management Team, Finance and Administration Committee, and Risk and Audit Committee;
Lead long-term financial planning, annual budgeting, forecasting, scenario analysis, and cash flow management;
Ensure WADA’s long-term financial sustainability through effective resource allocation, financial planning, reserves management, and risk management.

Accounting, Treasury & Financial Compliance

Maintain executive oversight of WADA’s accounting operations and ensure the integrity, accuracy, and timeliness of financial reporting;
Oversee all treasury and cash management activities in conjunction with WADA’s bankers, investment managers, and financial advisors, with particular attention to the prudent management of WADA’s cash reserves;
Ensure WADA’s compliance with applicable International Financial Reporting Standards (IFRS), Swiss legal and regulatory requirements, and relevant Canadian and Swiss tax obligations;
Establish, maintain, and continuously strengthen appropriate financial policies, internal controls, delegations, and governance frameworks to safeguard WADA’s financial assets.

Contribution, Funding & Financial Sustainability

Provide executive oversight of WADA’s contribution management framework, including budgeting, forecasting, collection, reporting, and compliance;
Develop financial models and scenarios to support WADA’s long-term funding requirements and sustainability;
Monitor contribution trends and advise executive leadership and governing bodies on funding risks, opportunities, and longer-term financial implications;
Ensure transparency, accountability, and sound stewardship in the management and reporting of WADA’s financial resources.

Enterprise Risk, Governance & Decision Support

Provide executive leadership on financial risk and contribute to WADA’s broader enterprise risk management framework;
Integrate financial, strategic, and risk considerations into major organizational decisions and recommendations;
Provide financial and strategic analysis to support significant investments, initiatives, partnerships, and organizational changes;
Advise the Director General and governing bodies on the financial and strategic implications of key decisions.

Leadership & Organizational Capacity

Lead the Finance and Strategy functions, including oversight of the Controller and the leaders and staff responsible for finance, procurement/managed services and organizational strategy;
Establish an effective organizational structure, accountabilities, processes, and capabilities within Finance and Strategy to support WADA’s objectives;
Build, develop, and retain high-performing teams with strong financial, analytical, strategic, and business-partnering capabilities;
Foster collaboration between Finance, Strategy, and WADA’s operational and program Groups.

Stakeholder Engagement, Board & Committee Reporting

Lead the preparation and presentation of financial and strategic information for the Foundation Board, Executive Committee, Finance and Administration Committee, senior management, contributors, and other stakeholders, as required;
Prepare for and provide executive leadership and support to meetings of the Finance and Administration Committee;
Participate in and support the Risk & Audit Committee (RAC), including preparation and presentation of key financial, risk, audit, and governance information;
Build trusted relationships with WADA’s stakeholders and provide transparent, credible information regarding WADA’s financial position, resource requirements, and strategic priorities.

WHAT WE'RE LOOKING FOR

Qualifications and Experience

University degree
in Finance, Accounting, Business Administration, Economics, or a related discipline; an advanced degree is considered an asset;
Recognized professional accounting or financial designation such as CPA, ACCA, CFA, or equivalent is required;
Senior management experience in financial leadership, including responsibility for financial planning, budgeting, reporting, treasury, audit, controls, risk management, and organizational decision support;
A minimum of 8 years
of progressively responsible experience, including substantial experience in a senior financial leadership capacity;
Demonstrated experience contributing to organizational strategy, strategic planning, enterprise performance management, and executive-level decision-making;
Experience leading multidisciplinary teams and senior professionals; experience overseeing both Finance and Strategy functions is an asset;
Experience working within an international, multi-stakeholder, non-profit, public-sector, sport, or comparable mission-driven environment is highly desirable;
Strong knowledge of International Financial Reporting Standards (IFRS), financial governance, internal controls, and risk management;
Demonstrated ability to advise senior executives and governing bodies on complex financial and strategic matters;
Strong analytical and business judgment, with the ability to connect financial performance, organizational performance, risk, and strategy;
Excellent communicator and presenter, with demonstrated ability to translate complex financial and performance information into clear narratives and actionable insights;
Strong experience with financial and enterprise systems, data analytics, and performance reporting tools;
Advanced Microsoft Office skills;
Fluency in either French or English, with good working knowledge of the other; additional language skills are an asset;
Fit with organizational culture: Teamwork, team spirit and love of sport;
Aligned with WADA core values: Integrity, Collaboration and Excellence.

WHAT WE OFFER

A Competitive Benefits Package.

Vision:
WADA’s vision is a world where all athletes compete in a doping-free sporting environment.
Mission:
WADA's mission is to lead a collaborative worldwide movement for doping-free sport.
About us:
WADA is headquartered in Montreal, Canada and has regional offices in Cape Town, South Africa; Lausanne, Switzerland; Montevideo, Uruguay; Tokyo, Japan and the office of the President in Warsaw, Poland. As of February 2026, the Agency employs approximately 177 employees and is represented by 55 nationalities. We value the diversity of our employees – current and future – that, as a global team, endeavor every day to protect the rights of clean athletes worldwide.

The masculine is used in our communications for the sole purpose of lightening the text and it designates all genders. WADA believes in the success of an inclusive organization that values diversity within its team. All qualified candidates will be considered for this position in a fair manner. WADA would like to thank all candidates who have shown an interest by applying for a position. However, after a thorough profile review, only the retained candidates will be contacted.

